      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(window): honor task cancellation while waiting for window disappear",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nCanceling `peekaboo window close` while it waited for disappearance could keep polling for the full timeout. Worse, treating cancellation as an ordinary timeout allowed the close flow to continue with focus, Cmd-W, Cmd-Shift-W, and pointer-click fallbacks after the caller had already stopped the command.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Propagate `CancellationError` from disappearance polling instead of returning a timeout result.\n- Check cancellation before and after presence reads and before every fallback side effect.\n- Explicitly cancel the MainActor window-service operation when the CLI bridge's parent task is canceled.\n- Replace the model-only proof script with deterministic production-helper and bridge tests.\n- Add contributor credit to the changelog.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `swift test --package-path Core/PeekabooAutomationKit --filter WindowDisappearanceCancellationTests` — 4 tests\n- [x] `swift test --package-path Apps/CLI --filter ServiceBridgeTests` — 13 tests\n- [x] `pnpm run format`\n- [x] `pnpm run lint` — 0 errors (13 pre-existing warnings)\n- [x] `pnpm run test:safe` — 747 tests / 85 suites\n- [x] `pnpm run test:automation` — 1,341 tests / 181 suites\n- [x] `pnpm run build:cli`\n- [x] Signed-host TextEdit smoke: permissions granted; exact fixture window closed and disappeared from `window list`\n- [x] Maintainer cleanup autoreview — no actionable findings\n- [x] Full branch autoreview — no actionable findings\n\n## Related\n\n- #267 — menu bar click cancellation\n- #230 — app running-state cancellation\n- #203 — daemon poll cancellation\n",
